YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(YuvMatrix, u8"YUV 矩阵", u8"YUV matrix")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(YuvMatrixHelp, u8"选择源素材使用的 YCbCr -> RGB 转换矩阵。\n选错可能导致颜色偏差；源原色与传输函数需在下方分别设置。", u8"Select the source YCbCr to RGB conversion matrix.\nAn incorrect matrix shifts colors. Set primaries and transfer function separately below.")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(ColorRangeHelp, u8"按源素材的量化范围解读 YUV 码值。\n8 位：Limited 为 Y 16-235、U/V 16-240；Full 为 0-255。\n10 位：Limited 为 Y 64-940、U/V 64-960；Full 为 0-1023。\n选错可能导致黑位发灰，或暗部与高光细节丢失。", u8"Interpret YUV code values using the source quantization range.\n8-bit: Limited Y 16-235, U/V 16-240; Full 0-255.\n10-bit: Limited Y 64-940, U/V 64-960; Full 0-1023.\nAn incorrect range can raise blacks or lose shadow and highlight detail.")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(FullColor, u8"彩色", u8"Color")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(DisplayChannel, u8"显示通道", u8"Channel")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(YuvChannelHelp, u8"彩色：将 YUV 转为 RGB，并应用下方色彩设置。\nY/U/V：以灰度查看所选分量，不应用下方色彩设置。\nY 按所选数值范围拉伸；U/V 按原始码值显示。", u8"Color: convert YUV to RGB and apply the color settings below.\nY/U/V: show the selected component as grayscale, without those settings.\nY uses the selected range; U/V show raw code values.")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(BayerChannelHelp, u8"R/G/B：以灰度查看 Bayer 插值后的对应分量。\nBayer 没有透明度通道，选择 A 时仍显示彩色图像。", u8"R/G/B: show the interpolated Bayer component as grayscale.\nBayer has no alpha channel; A still displays the color image.")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(GrayscaleChannelHelp, u8"灰度格式始终显示单通道图像，此选项不改变画面。\n下方色彩设置仍然生效。", u8"Grayscale formats always show one channel; this choice has no effect.\nThe color settings below still apply.")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(RgbChannelHelp, u8"彩色：显示 RGB，并应用下方色彩设置。\nR/G/B/A：以灰度查看所选分量，不应用下方色彩设置。\nA 表示透明度；没有透明度通道时显示白色。", u8"Color: display RGB and apply the color settings below.\nR/G/B/A: show one component as grayscale, without those settings.\nA is alpha; images without alpha display white.")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(HdrTransfer, u8"HDR / 传输函数", u8"HDR / Transfer")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(SourcePrimaries, u8"源原色", u8"Primaries")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(SourcePrimariesHelp, u8"选择源素材的 RGB 三原色，决定其色域含义。\n程序据此转换到输出所用的 RGB 色彩空间。\n请按素材信息选择；此项不会自动修改 YUV 矩阵或传输函数。", u8"Select the source RGB primaries to define its color space.\nThe image is converted from these primaries to the output color space.\nUse the source specification; YUV matrix and transfer function remain unchanged.")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(Linear, u8"线性", u8"Linear")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(TransferFunction, u8"传输函数", u8"Transfer")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(TransferFunctionHelp, u8"选择源素材的码值到线性光的转换方式。\nSDR 按 sRGB 解读；BT.1886 使用 gamma 2.4；线性表示码值已是线性光。\nPQ 按绝对亮度解读；HLG 还需结合下方 HLG 峰值。\n请按素材信息选择，P010 等像素格式本身不能确定传输函数。", u8"Select how source code values convert to linear light.\nSDR uses sRGB; BT.1886 uses gamma 2.4; Linear means values are already linear.\nPQ specifies absolute luminance; HLG also uses the peak setting below.\nUse the source specification. A pixel format such as P010 cannot determine this.")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(ReferenceWhite, u8"参考白 (nit)", u8"Ref. white (nit)")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(ReferenceWhiteHelp, u8"PQ/HLG 转为 SDR 显示时，将此亮度归一化为线性值 1.0，再做色调映射。\n默认 203 nit；调大使画面变暗，调小使画面变亮。1 nit = 1 cd/m²。\nHDR 输出生效时不使用此项；SDR、BT.1886、线性输入下不可调整。", u8"For PQ/HLG to SDR, this luminance becomes linear 1.0 before tone mapping.\nDefault: 203 nit. Higher values darken the image; lower values brighten it.\n1 nit = 1 cd/m². Not used for HDR output or SDR, BT.1886 and Linear input.")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(HlgPeak, u8"HLG 峰值 (nit)", u8"HLG peak (nit)")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(HlgPeakHelp, u8"将 HLG 信号转换为显示亮度时采用的标称峰值，默认 1000 nit。\n它同时影响亮度尺度与系统 gamma，因此会改变画面的亮度和对比度。\n此值需手动指定，不会自动跟随当前显示器峰值。", u8"Nominal peak used to convert HLG to display luminance; default 1000 nit.\nIt affects both luminance scale and system gamma, changing brightness and contrast.\nSet it manually; it does not follow the current display peak.")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(ToneMapping, u8"色调映射", u8"Tone mapping")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(ToneMappingHelp, u8"选择 SDR 输出时的亮度映射方式，非 SDR 传输函数下可调整。\n裁剪：直接截断超出范围的值；Reinhard：压缩高光，可调映射白点；\nACES：使用电影风格的近似曲线压缩亮度。\nHDR 输出生效时不使用此项，而是按显示器峰值限制高光。", u8"Luminance mapping for SDR output; adjustable for non-SDR transfer functions.\nClip truncates values; Reinhard compresses highlights with an adjustable white point.\nACES uses a film-like approximation curve.\nHDR output instead limits highlights to the display peak.")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(MappingWhite, u8"映射白点", u8"White point")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(MappingWhiteHelp, u8"Reinhard 曲线中映射到输出白色（1.0）的线性输入值。\nPQ/HLG 转 SDR 时以参考白为单位，并在曝光调整后计算。\n数值越大，高光压缩越强；仅用于 SDR 输出的 Reinhard 映射。", u8"Linear input mapped to output white (1.0) by the Reinhard curve.\nFor PQ/HLG to SDR, measured in reference-white units after exposure adjustment.\nHigher values compress highlights more. Only used by Reinhard for SDR output.")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(Exposure, u8"曝光 (档)", u8"Exposure (EV)")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(ExposureHelp, u8"在色调映射或高光限幅前调整线性亮度。\n+1 档为原来的 2 倍，-1 档为原来的 1/2；0 档不调整。\nSDR 与 HDR 输出均适用。", u8"Adjust linear luminance before tone mapping or highlight limiting.\n+1 EV doubles luminance; -1 EV halves it; 0 leaves it unchanged.\nApplies to both SDR and HDR output.")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(HighlightOutOfRange, u8"超范围高亮", u8"Highlight out of range")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(HighlightOutOfRangeHelp, u8"在色调映射与裁剪前，用颜色标记超范围的 RGB 分量。\n红色：任一分量超过当前输出路径的上限。\n蓝色：任一分量为负，可能来自超黑或原色转换；红色优先。\n负分量不一定超出实际显示器色域，HDR 输出可保留负值。", u8"Mark out-of-range RGB values before tone mapping and clipping.\nRed: any component exceeds the output limit.\nBlue: any component is negative, from super-black or primary conversion; red wins.\nNegative values need not be outside the display gamut; HDR can preserve them.")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(HdrOutput, u8"HDR 输出", u8"HDR output")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(HdrOutputHelp, u8"为主窗口启用 HDR 输出，主图与对比图共用此开关。\nPQ/HLG 按解读后的亮度输出，仍受曝光与显示器峰值限制。\n关闭后按 SDR 显示；拖出主窗口的图像面板始终按 SDR 显示。", u8"Enable HDR output for the main window, including both images.\nPQ/HLG use interpreted luminance, subject to exposure and display peak limits.\nWhen disabled, output is SDR. Detached image windows always use SDR.")
YUVRAW_UI_TEXT(HdrUnavailableHelp, u8"%s\n\nHDR 输出需要显示器开启 HDR，且程序的 HDR 通路可用。\n若当前显示器未开启 HDR，可在系统设置中开启，或将主窗口移到已开启 HDR 的显示器。", u8"%s\n\nHDR requires an HDR-enabled display and a working HDR output path.\nEnable HDR in Windows or move the main window to an HDR-enabled display.")
